WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.616
Hi, I'm Ratline!

00:00:02.616 --> 00:00:06.240
SpatialScout drops an agent into a room it has never seen and

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.448
asks for a map.

00:00:07.448 --> 00:00:09.260
Here's how that map is graded.

00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:13.546
The agent submits one centre per object.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:17.934
The scorer slides the true box onto that point and measures the overlap.

00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:25.465
The agent gets object IDs and categories, and one image.

00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:26.240
No positions.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.590
It moves a calibrated camera and captures new views, up to a hundred.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.133
For depth, it marks one feature in two views, and the

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.269
tool intersects the rays.

00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:39.231
It submits a centre per object, and revises as it explores.

00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:42.578
Only afterwards does the scorer compare the map with the truth.

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:45.898
Same size boxes, one axis.

00:00:46.318 --> 00:00:49.899
Shift a box of side L by d, and L minus d still overlaps.

00:00:50.319 --> 00:00:51.895
Together they span L plus d.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.691
So above zero point nine needs an offset under a nineteenth of the side.

00:00:57.691 --> 00:01:00.052
For a thin painting, a millimetre or two.

00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:04.642
I ran the released scorer on maps I built.

00:01:04.642 --> 00:01:08.124
Five centimetres of noise everywhere scores about thirty seven percent.

00:01:08.124 --> 00:01:10.562
The best agent scores about forty two.

00:01:11.775 --> 00:01:13.690
The authors read forty runs.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.456
Six succeeded.

00:01:14.876 --> 00:01:17.648
Most failed runs stopped before finding everything.

00:01:18.068 --> 00:01:20.795
Many submitted a wrong point though the rays met cleanly.

00:01:21.221 --> 00:01:23.061
Some kept points the tool had flagged.

00:01:25.092 --> 00:01:25.750
One catch.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:29.697
In the released code, a perfect map with chairs filed under each

00:01:29.697 --> 00:01:31.670
other's IDs scores seventy nine percent.

00:01:33.142 --> 00:01:35.066
A low residual proves the rays met.

00:01:35.066 --> 00:01:37.266
Not that they met on the object's centre.

00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:43.481
Drive the camera and triangulate.

00:01:43.481 --> 00:01:45.868
The true box slides onto each point.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.597
The best agent lands a few centimetres off.

00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.083
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:51.673
I'm Ratline.

00:01:51.673 --> 00:01:51.968
Bye!
